WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.682
This example creates a common table expression called older patients.

00:00:04.682 --> 00:00:08.617
The first stage keeps patients who are older than fifty.

00:00:08.617 --> 00:00:13.047
At that point, one row still represents one patient.

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:19.747
The final part joins those patients to admissions and counts how many admissions each patient has.

00:00:19.747 --> 00:00:25.477
Notice that the query becomes easier to explain because the filtering step has a name.

00:00:25.477 --> 00:00:31.930
We can first verify which patients are in the intermediate result, and then reason about the join and the count.
